          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part I"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.107,
            0.885,
            0.148
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is the journey over? Are there more numbers waiting to be discovered beyond the Real Number line?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.173,
            0.399,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.21,
            0.872,
            0.286
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider this puzzle: What is the square root of –1? We know that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 \\times 1 = 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We also know that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( - 1 ) \\times ( - 1 ) = 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " There is no Real Number that, when multiplied by itself, results in a negative number. Thus, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\sqrt { - 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " cannot exist on number line."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.313,
            0.886,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To solve this, mathematicians stepped completely off the line and invented a new dimension of numbers, denoted by the letter i, standing for "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Imaginary Numbers",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". While they sound like fiction, they are essential for modern electrical engineering, quantum mechanics, and the technology that powers your mobile phone. But that is a journey for another year. For now, master the Real Numbers. The universe is largely written in their language."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.304,
            0.487,
            0.692,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "End-of-Chapter Exercises"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.532,
            0.885,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Convert the following rational numbers in the form of a terminating decimal or non-terminating and repeating decimal, whichever the case may be, by the process of long division: (i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 5 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{2}{9}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.64,
            0.605,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Prove that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\sqrt { 5 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is an irrational number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.676,
            0.807,
            0.807
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Convert the following decimal numbers in the form of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { p } { q } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (i) 12.6 (ii) 0.0120 (iii) 3.052 (iv) 1.235 (v) 0.23 (vi) 2.05 (vii) 2.125 (viii) 3.125 (ix) 2.1625"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
